Z||000000||moonie||07-29-2000||02:54 PM||||85 se 4 cyl.<P>was leaking water into the oil & onto the ground. so i'm removing the head to check if warped or gasket blow out. i've removed everything on the carb side. i think all thats left is the exhaust manifold & the water pump. then i will be ready to remove the head. ( i think ) <P>question.....<BR>do i have to take off the tappings & push rods & springs or will they not matter to  lift the head  off the block ?<BR>and if i do have to remove them , is there anything i should be wary of or do beforehand ?<P>thanks <BR>moonster||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||07-30-2000||10:10 AM||||I would remove the push rods, but the lifters can stay in if that's what you mean by tappings.  No the springs do not have to come off to remove the head.  Just loosen the rocker arm nuts and turn them to get the push rods out.  While you have the head off, it would be a real good idea to take it to a machine shop and have it magna fluxed to check for cracks. The heads with the "v" chambers in them, are notorious for cracking across the webbing. <P>Hope this helps.<P>Have a good one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
